:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-56-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2050009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e7daa5fb1e6656b1c047ea1313ec597a00316cba3e24c5fdabdf673ad5664b67","compact":"5092354dc2ad19c5a451ae03af4726a7979fbce9ef6be4f93fa9fc5cdb22f4de","nasal":"5092354dc2ad19c5a451ae03af4726a7979fbce9ef6be4f93fa9fc5cdb22f4de"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-50-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":50,"verse":10,"english":"Do you behold Citrakuta frequented by mad elephants and resonant with the voice of multitudes of birds, the mountain with its towering summits.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.934,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-56-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2050010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7d4ee85a1e0b4b1ecf8c0f03645bd9c17272e2c9ffafc50737b1e3db6e2f4aa8","compact":"ad7de75594b5149a5099aa053a839084a0645050802e5a01005df8f31d2f5167","nasal":"ad7de75594b5149a5099aa053a839084a0645050802e5a01005df8f31d2f5167"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-50-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":50,"verse":11,"english":"Then they proceeding on foot along with Sītā, arrived at the charming and beautiful mountain Citrakuta.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-56-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2050011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c16b3857cd8edddae085f801d54a0f6670db06fde47d59d9b67c5817ac41af50","compact":"763ecfacbb6cebc6d6921b31c09690081eee4f6bd9ee3416a0d48eec6eec428e","nasal":"64fe14c9658a8b399ce7911c795767bd1ffe67dde62f2c29da79bac68074ad43"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-50-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":50,"verse":12,"english":"Arriving at the mountain inhabited by birds of various kinds, abounding in fruits and roots, and furnished with watery expanses, (Răma) said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.464,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-56-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2050012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21eaf612b3c4bca1069891b53ace97446231f941b382090d02ec36e442c37271","compact":"173737f07742977b9b33348069184f7b8a0104584c1ea34da948c9598d34d6c7","nasal":"173737f07742977b9b33348069184f7b8a0104584c1ea34da948c9598d34d6c7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-50-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":50,"verse":13,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, bring you wood good and strong. O amiable one, construct a dwelling. My mind is set upon staying here.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-56-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2050013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c45091aa6f582bb1676156484b844d012cc2ce29f0e73afc864f01722d2253b","compact":"04372631c3e5e8ab98484cd9956f0c1709fa3be5be8d635e6a96bc4284803984","nasal":"04372631c3e5e8ab98484cd9956f0c1709fa3be5be8d635e6a96bc4284803984"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-50-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":50,"verse":14,"english":"Hearing his words, Sumitra's son procured woods of various descriptions, and then that subduer of foes reared a cottage thatched with leaves.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-56-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2050014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"248cec28c3d529eb8b031bd86af90a09ecb874c90b69618a19da49a3b97a9516","compact":"4245182174b13b4c5a94d907a3205f0542e121aacfc4a368c63ae01801a87243","nasal":"5162a618eac07851af1c81dccb1639bd1febacb43e4d6a3f0d6348ba3cbfe454"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-50-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":50,"verse":15,"english":"Beholding that goodly dwelling walled with wood furnished with doors, Rāma addressed these words and Lakşmaņa, intent upon ministering to his brother. Procuring meat, we will worship the deity presiding over this dwelling. O Sumitrā's son, those who wish to live long, should pacify the household gods.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.467,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-56-20","DUTT-2-56-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2050015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"528361659e578098186364cfe0770497a6390c0749582da4f5cacd70968fdfaf","compact":"64855020319094e36386d495b42939f05f03ea91ea0aa83242c8d67e75e44ade","nasal":"64855020319094e36386d495b42939f05f03ea91ea0aa83242c8d67e75e44ade"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-50-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":50,"verse":16,"english":"Then Lakşmana the son of Sumitrā endowed with vigour, having slain a sacred black deer, threw it into flaming fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.762,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-56-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2050016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4a508da9f8b71862711bc5be2867e8b6ab64ca92db9bfc4be2af4e272c81ac9b","compact":"b27849e408f7683332e22b7eb0a5fd796f3c2475dd502bfd9f0cf5e5566ec4e6","nasal":"b27849e408f7683332e22b7eb0a5fd796f3c2475dd502bfd9f0cf5e5566ec4e6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-50-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":50,"verse":17,"english":"And seeing it well scorched and hot and free from blood, Lakşmaņa spoke to that foremost of men, Rāghava, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.969,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-56-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2050017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":